00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.680
Best practices.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.460
The biggest misconception

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.280
when it comes to prompt engineering

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:51.560
is that it's an easy job with no science to it.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.640
I imagine a lot of people think

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:56.320
it's just about constructing a one-off sentence

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.300
such as correct my paragraph

00:20:58.300 --> 00:21:00.640
that we saw in the previous example.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:01.960
When you start to look at it,

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:03.640
creating effective prompts

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:06.560
relies on a bunch of different factors.

00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.120
Here are some things to consider

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.240
when writing a good prompt.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.760
Consider writing clear instructions

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:14.800
with details in your query.

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.920
Consider adopting a persona

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.480
as well as specifying the format

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:21.800
using iterative prompting,

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:24.160
meaning if you have a multi-part question

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.420
or if the first response wasn't sufficient,

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:28.880
you can continue by asking follow-up questions

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:31.320
or asking the model to elaborate

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.660
and avoid leading the answer.

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:35.560
Try not to make your prompts so leading

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.600
that it inadvertently tells the model

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:39.520
what answer you're expecting.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.480
This might bias the response unduly.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:45.380
And finally, limit the scope for long topics.

00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.080
If you're asking about a broad topic,

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.360
it's helpful to break it down

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:51.460
or limit the scope to get a more focused answer.

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.600
Let's look at some of these now.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.760
In order to write clearer instructions,

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:59.240
we can adopt writing more details in our queries.

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:00.720
And to get the best results,

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.460
don't assume the AI knows what you are talking about.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:07.320
Writing something like, when is the election,

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:10.360
implies that you are expecting the AI to know

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:12.320
what election you are talking about

00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:14.160
and what country you mean.

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:17.500
This may result in you asking a few follow-up questions

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.560
to finally get the result you want,

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.680
resulting in time loss and frankly,

00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:23.560
perhaps some frustration.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.880
Consider taking the time to write a prompt

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:27.540
with clear instructions.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:30.240
So, for example, instead of writing,

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:32.560
when is the election, you could write,

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:36.440
when is the next presidential election for Poland?

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:39.320
So let's go ahead and run this.

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:41.840
And this will be much more precise

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:44.920
and knows exactly what we are asking about.

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:48.400
It's not gonna go guessing and waste our time

00:22:48.400 --> 00:22:50.440
as well as waste our resources.

00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:52.800
So in other words, tokens that we are using,

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:54.620
so in other words, money,

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:57.240
in order to get the right answer the first time.

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:59.000
Here are some other examples

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.760
of how you could write clearer prompts.

00:23:01.760 --> 00:23:03.980
So for example, we have this prompt here,

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:07.640
which says write code to filter out the ages from data.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:09.260
And if you run it,

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:10.520
you don't really know what language

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.640
it's gonna come back with, let's see.

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:15.560
So for example, here it's using Python.

00:23:15.560 --> 00:23:18.120
I actually didn't wanna use Python, okay?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:21.600
So now we've lost some tokens asking this.

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:23.720
We've also lost some time

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:25.720
and we just haven't got the right response.

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:28.240
This could have been so easily avoided.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:30.680
So I'm gonna stop this from generating

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.640
and let's try again.

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:36.480
So this time, let's be more specific by writing,

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:38.120
write a JavaScript function

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:40.000
that will take an array of objects

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.840
and filter out the value of age property

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:44.720
and put them in a new array.

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:47.640
Please explain what each code snippet does.

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:50.360
In this example, I am not assuming the AI knows

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.600
what computer language I like to use

00:23:52.600 --> 00:23:54.420
and I am being more specific

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:56.700
about what my data actually looks like.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:59.760
On this occasion, it's an array of objects.

00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:02.800
Not only that, I'm also asking the AI

00:24:02.800 --> 00:24:05.200
to explain why it's doing each step

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:07.480
so that I in turn can understand

00:24:07.480 --> 00:24:08.880
and not just copy paste the code

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:11.160
without gaining any knowledge from it.

00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.840
Okay, so here you can see a live example

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:17.840
of what's coming back to us from GPT-4.

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.440
It's given us the correct code.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:21.800
So I have checked that

00:24:21.800 --> 00:24:24.160
and I was also giving us an example

00:24:24.160 --> 00:24:25.960
of how you would use the function,

00:24:25.960 --> 00:24:27.360
which is something I didn't ask,

00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:28.720
which is super useful.

00:24:28.720 --> 00:24:30.800
It's kind of gone above and beyond

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:34.820
for helping me out in understanding what is going on.

00:24:35.880 --> 00:24:37.880
Let's look at another example.

00:24:37.880 --> 00:24:41.720
We can write, tell me what this essay is about.

00:24:41.720 --> 00:24:44.000
So I'm going to just type this

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:46.500
and then just paste in an essay and hit go.

00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:49.400
And then chat GPT will do its thing.

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:51.960
It's going to give me a summarization

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:53.800
as it thinks best.

00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:55.000
So on this occasion,

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:57.880
it is essentially giving me numbered points

00:24:57.880 --> 00:25:00.240
about what this essay is about.

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:01.200
They're really long.

00:25:01.200 --> 00:25:03.560
I really didn't want to read this much.

00:25:03.560 --> 00:25:06.680
It's pretty much looking to be the same

00:25:06.680 --> 00:25:08.600
as the original essay.

00:25:08.600 --> 00:25:11.160
So this is not something I wanted.

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:13.200
I should have been way more specific

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:14.960
in telling it what I need.

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:19.480
So what I'm going to do is just add to this conversation.

00:25:19.480 --> 00:25:22.520
So it's going to learn on what I wrote previously.

00:25:22.520 --> 00:25:24.760
And I'm just going to specify to use bullet points

00:25:24.760 --> 00:25:27.060
to explain what this essay is about,

00:25:27.060 --> 00:25:30.020
making sure each point is no longer the 10 words long.

00:25:30.020 --> 00:25:33.360
So I am being super specific

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:37.440
in providing the instructions of what I want

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.080
